All 8 runs scored 0 on dev, and training success was also about 0 (0 to 0.0002). There were no 0.078 collapses. Under the program's rules, this means the action layout is still unmatched. It is not a collapse or a generalisation problem. Candidate r1c2 already covered the 8 dihedral frames, anchor offsets within the centred window, free type slots and both type-major and anchor-major orders. So the mismatch is probably outside that family. Candidates still open:
- an index shift such as DONE first or a roll of ±1;
- the middle-type order (y, t, x);
- per-type frames combined with free window slots;
- obs channel groups sitting in different frames;
- footprints or anchor offsets beyond ±1;
- an arbitrary permutation.

This round keeps breadth. A is a factorised head: per-type frames × 3 orders × 3 index shifts. B, C and D each add one hypothesis on top of A (obs frames, a learned dense remap, a wider reach), so a hit points to its cause. The recipe stays at the default.
